    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23212" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infirmātĭo</span></b> , ōnis.
			f.
		1. infirmo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a weakening</i>, <i>invalidating.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Rerum judicatarum, <i><span class="en">Cic. Agr. 2,
				3, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 4, 10</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a refuting</i>,
				<i>disproving</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">judicatio est, quae ex infirmatione et
					confirmatione rationis nascitur controversia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Inv. 1, 13, 18</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 21, 62</span></i>.</div>
